# Line endings are part of the build here, not cosmetics.
#
# The check scripts in web/scripts/ parse the source files as text with hard
# '\n' anchors — check-journey.mjs, for instance, reads the cast table out of
# placements.ts with /\],?\n/. On a Windows clone with git's default
# core.autocrlf=true the checkout rewrites every line to CRLF, that regex stops
# matching, the cast table reads as empty, and `npm run verify` fails with 16
# false "speaker has no placement" errors on a tree that is actually correct.
#
# The blobs in this repo are already LF, so pinning the checkout to LF costs
# nothing and removes the trap.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets are bytes — never let the text filter near them.
*.glb  binary
*.gltf binary
*.fbx  binary
*.blend binary
*.vdb  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.hdr  binary
*.exr  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
